
Code for a new take on the use of avx512.
Vector of uint32_t will be replaced with a single uint64_t pointer.
All members of the uint32_t vector will be > 0 at all times.
and a vector of pointers to uin64_t 8 elements apart (512 bits).

Allocation will be through aligned_allocator.
To detect if the processor supports AVX512, 
use the __cpuid function from cpuid.h header.

The assembly algorithm for add and subtract should 
be changed to generate the masks on the fly 
instead of doing a load. 

Scatter/gather is not a good substitute for permute
instructions since it does not allow for jumping lanes.

